       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the maximum.\n\n- **Requested:** 1700 mg three times daily = 5,100 mg/day\n- **Maximum for immediate-release metformin:** 2,550 mg/day (typically 850 mg three times daily), even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nEntering a dose twice the maximum could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber. Even if the dose were correct, I can't enter it on the word of a non-clinician, so the order should go through the medicine team.\n\nPossible next steps:\n- A prescriber on the medicine service reviews the order and confirms the intended dose. It may be a typo, for example 850 mg or 500 mg three times daily, or 1700 mg once daily if it's extended-release (the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day).\n- If a prescriber confirms a dose at or below the maximum, I can enter it, with a note recording the prescriber's name."
